              "type": "text",
              "text": "Consider the number 18. It has six factors: 1, 2, 3, 6, 9, 18. We can count the number of factors by using the powers of the prime factorisation:",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p64-q29-teaching-factorisation",
