        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$12$",
          "worked": "There are 4 choices for the power of 2 and 3 choices for the power of 3.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\text{Number of factors}&=(3+1)(2+1)\\\\&=12\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 14
      },
      {
        "id": "p64-q29-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$1\\,000\\,000$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$49$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}1\\,000\\,000&=10^6\\\\&=2^6\\cdot5^6\\end{aligned}$$\nEach prime exponent has 7 choices.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\text{Number of factors}&=(6+1)(6+1)\\\\&=49\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p64-q29-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$315\\,000$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$120$",
          "worked": "$$315\\,000=2^3\\cdot3^2\\cdot5^4\\cdot7$$\nThe powers of the four primes have 4, 3, 5 and 2 choices respectively.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\text{Number of factors}&=(3+1)(2+1)(4+1)(1+1)\\\\&=120\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 19
      },
      {
        "id": "p64-q29-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$2^a\\times5^b\\times13^c$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(a+1)(b+1)(c+1)$",
          "worked": "The power of 2 has $a+1$ choices, the power of 5 has $b+1$ choices, and the power of 13 has $c+1$ choices. Therefore,\n$$\\text{Number of factors}=(a+1)(b+1)(c+1).$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 15
      }
    ]
